  "id": "triad",
  "term": "triad",
  "definition": "In this psychology context, the triad refers to the Dark Triad: three related but distinct personality traits—psychopathy, Machiavellianism, and narcissism. They overlap in tendencies such as manipulativeness and low empathy, but differ in style, with psychopathy described as more reckless, Machiavellianism more calculated, and narcissism more centered on grandiosity and admiration.",
